## Delineation

& [Inside] is future bounded hardware work
  + [shared_protocol] is the canonical CantorQueryRequest, CantorQueryResult, package, proof, fault, and digest machine forms
  + [interpretive_profile] is a stable hardware or soft-core semantic virtual machine consuming compiled signed Cantor bytecode packages
  + [native_profile] is a compiler lowering a frozen bounded Cantor plan and admitted fabric projection through a hardware IR to synthesizable RTL and a target bitstream
  + [accelerator_candidate] is digest verification, exact hash lookup, typed adjacency traversal, boundary filtering, candidate scoring, and proof-trace event generation
  + [host_control] is software package admission, device loading, lifecycle policy, result verification, and fault handling unless later proof safely relocates them

& [Outside] is not implied by offering FPGA support
  + [raw_SOP_execution] is uncompiled or unsigned text interpreted as authority
  + [arbitrary_SOP_synthesis] is unrestricted language-to-circuit compilation
  + [self_modifying_hardware] is runtime logic mutation outside governed partial-reconfiguration protocol
  + [neural_authority] is learned weights resolving or authorizing meaning
  + [device_selection] is a vendor, board, capacity, clock, interface, or tool license commitment
  + [production_security] is a claim that test signing, bitstream encryption, or secure boot is production-safe without a target threat model

& [Uncertainty] is retained by the future slice
  + [hardware_target] is vendor, device family, board, toolchain, and host interface
  + [IR_path] is handwritten RTL, HLS, CIRCT or MLIR lowering, or a constrained combination
  + [bytecode] is opcode set, width, memory model, control flow, fault semantics, and versioning
  + [resource_model] is block RAM, LUT, DSP, routing, clock, bandwidth, power, and reconfiguration cost
  + [trust_partition] is which admission and verification steps occur on host, programmable logic, or both

## Shared Hardware Contract

& [FPGAExecutionEnvelope] is the immutable target binding
  + [protocol_digest] is the Cantor machine-form protocol digest
  + [compiler_digest] is the compiler and lowering-pipeline identity
  + [toolchain_digest] is synthesis, place, route, and bitstream tool identity
  + [target_digest] is device, board, interface, clock, and constraint identity
  + [package_digest] is the admitted semantic package or allowed package schema identity
  + [plan_digest] is the interpreted bytecode version or native query-plan identity
  + [bitstream_digest] is the produced device image identity
  + [equivalence_profile] is the software-oracle comparison contract
  = must: make every result traceable to this envelope

& [SoftwareReferenceOracle] is the safe-Rust Cantor core
  = must: remain the semantic acceptance oracle until FPGA equivalence is proven
  = must: run identical normalized requests and admitted packages against software and hardware profiles
  = must: compare normalized records, boundary accounts, relation paths, faults, omissions, quotes, and result digests
  - never: waive a mismatch as a harmless optimization without an explicit semantic proof

## Profile One: FPGA Interpreter

& [FPGAInterpretiveProfile] is a stable programmable semantic machine
  + [input] is versioned Cantor bytecode plus an admitted package projection
  + [hardware_shape] is finite-state control or a soft processor, bounded memories, exact indexes, typed traversal units, boundary gates, and trace output
  + [update_model] is load a new recognized bytecode or data package without resynthesizing the bitstream
  + [strength] is flexibility across SOP packages and query plans
  + [cost] is instruction dispatch, wider control state, and lower specialization than native circuits
  + [best_first_use] is prove hardware execution semantics and measure real bottlenecks
  = must: define bounded execution, instruction count, memory, traversal, and output budgets
  = must: reject unknown opcodes, protocol versions, packages, and authority scopes visibly

& [InterpreterInstructionFamilies] is candidate bytecode structure
  + [admission] is CHECK_ENVELOPE, CHECK_PACKAGE, and CHECK_SCOPE
  + [focus] is RESOLVE_TERM, FILTER_SUBJECT, FILTER_PURPOSE, FILTER_USE_CASE, INCLUDE_BOUNDARY, and EXCLUDE_BOUNDARY
  + [graph] is FOLLOW_RELATION, ADMIT_CANDIDATE, REJECT_CANDIDATE, and LIMIT_DEPTH
  + [source] is RESOLVE_ANCHOR and VERIFY_SPAN
  + [proof] is TRACE_DECISION, TRACE_FAULT, EMIT_RECORD, EMIT_PATH, EMIT_OMISSION, and FINALIZE_DIGEST
  + [control] is bounded branch, bounded loop, yield, and stop
  = must: derive final opcode names and encodings only after the software IR stabilizes

## Profile Two: Native FPGA

& [FPGANativeProfile] is a specialized circuit generated from a bounded Cantor plan
  + [input] is stable semantic IR, fixed query-plan subset, admitted fabric projection, target profile, and hardware constraints
  + [lowering] is Cantor IR to hardware-oriented IR to RTL or HLS output to synthesis, place, route, and bitstream
  + [hardware_shape] is pipelined and parallel exact-lookup, boundary, traversal, verification, or scoring datapaths
  + [update_model] is recompile and resynthesize when bound plan, fabric, target, or governing package changes
  + [strength] is throughput, predictable latency, and specialization
  + [cost] is long compile time, device specificity, reduced flexibility, and larger verification obligation
  + [best_first_use] is specialize one measured hotspot after the interpreter or software baseline identifies it
  = must: limit native lowering to a statically bounded synthesizable subset
  = must: reject dynamic allocation, recursion, unbounded graph walk, unbounded result growth, and unspecified timing

& [HardwareLoweringPipeline] is the native transform
  + [stage_1] is validate signed source package and canonical Cantor IR
  + [stage_2] is freeze permitted query-plan and authority envelope
  + [stage_3] is specialize widths, relation sets, memory maps, traversal limits, and budgets
  + [stage_4] is lower to explicit control, datapath, stream, memory, and interface IR
  + [stage_5] is emit synthesizable RTL directly or through a reviewed HLS path
  + [stage_6] is simulate and compare against the software oracle
  + [stage_7] is synthesize, place, route, and record timing and resource reports
  + [stage_8] is load hardware, run hardware-in-loop fixtures, and verify result digests
  + [stage_9] is sign or recognize the complete FPGAExecutionEnvelope

## Trust, Proof, and Failure

& [HardwareTrustBoundary] is stricter than ordinary execution
  + [threat] is stale, substituted, downgraded, or corrupted bitstream
  + [threat] is package and bitstream digest mismatch
  + [threat] is compiler or vendor-tool nondeterminism
  + [threat] is timing failure, memory overflow, deadlock, or interface backpressure
  + [threat] is partial-reconfiguration boundary violation
  + [threat] is fault or proof event loss under throughput pressure
  + [threat] is side-channel leakage of protected semantic material
  = must: fail closed on envelope, scope, digest, timing-health, memory, or protocol mismatch
  = must: preserve visible deterministic software fallback

& [FPGAEquivalenceProof] is the minimum evidence ladder
  + [level_1] is Rust reference fixture proof
  + [level_2] is bytecode-interpreter software model equivalence
  + [level_3] is RTL or HLS simulation equivalence
  + [level_4] is C-to-RTL or IR-to-RTL co-simulation where applicable
  + [level_5] is synthesis timing and resource acceptance
  + [level_6] is hardware-in-loop semantic and fault equivalence
  + [level_7] is cross-profile interpreter, native, and Rust normalized-result equivalence
  = must: retain counterexamples and mismatches as OperationalFaults

## Atomic Requirements

& [FPGARequirementSet] is the later feature collection
  + [CEB-021] is preserve one versioned Cantor protocol across Rust, interpreter FPGA, and native FPGA
  + [CEB-022] is define FPGAExecutionEnvelope and fail closed on every binding mismatch
  + [CEB-023] is define a bounded Cantor bytecode and software interpreter model
  + [CEB-024] is implement one FPGA interpreter target only after bytecode and software equivalence stabilize
  + [CEB-025] is define a statically synthesizable Cantor hardware subset and lowering contract
  + [CEB-026] is compile one measured deterministic query kernel through hardware IR or HLS to RTL
  + [CEB-027] is prove normalized result, proof, omission, and fault equivalence at every evidence level
  + [CEB-028] is record latency, throughput, area, memory, power estimate, compile time, and reconfiguration cost
  + [CEB-029] is preserve signed-package authority, mandatory gates, exact source resolution, and software fallback
  + [CEB-030] is prevent FPGA acceleration and neural routing from jointly bypassing deterministic authority

